  }}
  .kpi-card.accent {{ border-top-color: var(--red-600); }}
  .kpi-card.green {{ border-top-color: var(--green-600); }}
  .kpi-card.amber {{ border-top-color: var(--amber-500); }}
  .kpi-card .kpi-value {{
    font-size: 28px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--blue-900);
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }}
  .kpi-card .kpi-unit {{
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--gray-500);
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }}
  .kpi-card .kpi-label {{
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--gray-700);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.5px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }}

  /* Sections */
  .section {{
    padding: 40px 56px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gray-200);
  }}
  .section:last-child {{ border-bottom: none; }}
  .section h2 {{
    font-size: 24px;
    color: var(--blue-900);
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    font-weight: 700;
  }}
  .section .section-objective {{
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--gray-500);
    margin-bottom: 28px;
    font-style: italic;
  }}
  .section h3 {{
    font-size: 18px;
    color: var(--gray-700);
    margin: 28px 0 12px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }}
  .section p {{
    font-size: 15px;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
    color: var(--gray-900);
  }}

  /* Chart containers */
  .chart-box {{
    margin: 24px 0;
    background: var(--white);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 20px;
    border: 1px solid var(--gray-200);
  }}
  .chart-box .chart-title {{
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--gray-700);
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.5px;
  }}
  .chart-box canvas {{
    max-height: 380px;
  }}

  /* Two-column charts */
  .chart-row {{
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 20px;
  }}

  /* Tables */
  .data-table {{
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 14px;
    margin: 16px 0;
  }}
  .data-table th {{
    background: var(--blue-900);
    color: var(--white);
    padding: 10px 14px;
    text-align: left;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 12px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.5px;
  }}
  .data-table td {{
    padding: 10px 14px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gray-200);
  }}
  .data-table tr:nth-child(even) {{ background: var(--gray-100); }}
  .data-table .improver {{ color: var(--green-600); font-weight: 600; }}
  .data-table .deteriorator {{ color: var(--red-600); font-weight: 600; }}

  /* Callout box */
  .callout {{
    background: var(--blue-50);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--blue-500);
    padding: 16px 20px;
    margin: 20px 0;
    border-radius: 0 6px 6px 0;
    font-size: 14px;
  }}
  .callout.warning {{
    background: #fff8e6;
    border-left-color: var(--amber-500);
  }}
  .callout strong {{
    color: var(--blue-900);
  }}

  /* Footer */
  .report-footer {{
    padding: 32px 56px;
    background: var(--gray-900);
    color: var(--gray-500);
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }}
  .report-footer strong {{ color: var(--gray-200); }}

  /* Legend */
  .legend-inline {{
    display: flex;
    gap: 20px;
    font-size: 13px;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }}
  .legend-dot {{
    display: inline-block;
    width: 12px;
    height: 12px;
    border-radius: 2px;
    margin-right: 4px;
    vertical-align: middle;
  }}

  /* Bullet list */
  .insight-list {{
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
  }}
  .insight-list li {{
    padding: 8px 0 8px 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gray-200);
    position: relative;
    font-size: 14px;
  }}
  .insight-list li::before {{
    content: "▸";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--blue-500);
    font-size: 12px;
  }}

  @media (max-width: 900px) {{
    .kpi-dashboard {{ grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }}
    .chart-row {{ grid-template-columns: 1fr; }}
    .section {{ padding: 24px 20px; }}
    .report-header {{ padding: 32px 20px; }}
    .kpi-dashboard {{ padding: 20px; }}
  }}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="report-container">

<!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- HEADER -->
<!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<header class="report-header">
  <div class="tag">Trend Analysis Report</div>
  <h1>Global Intentional Homicide Trends<br>A Multi-Dimensional Analysis (1990–2023)</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">A comprehensive analysis of intentional homicide rates across countries, sexes, and age groups over three decades, drawing on United Nations Office on Drugs and Crime (UNODC) data.</p>
  <div class="meta">Data Source: UNODC Crime Trends Survey &middot; Coverage: 201 countries/territories &middot; Period: 1990–2023 &middot; Generated: May 2026</div>
</header>

<!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- KPI DASHBOARD -->
<!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="kpi-dashboard">
  <div class="kpi-card green">
    <div class="kpi-value">{kpis['global_median']}</div>
    <div class="kpi-unit">per 100,000</div>
    <div class="kpi-label">Global Median Homicide Rate ({kpis['max_year']})</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi-card accent">
    <div class="kpi-value">{kpis['mf_ratio']}:1</div>
    <div class="kpi-unit">Male : Female</div>
    <div class="kpi-label">Male-to-Female Homicide Rate Ratio</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi-card accent">
    <div class="kpi-value">{kpis['highest_national']['rate']}</div>
    <div class="kpi-unit">per 100,000</div>
    <div class="kpi-label">Highest National Rate — {kpis['highest_national']['country']}</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi-card amber">
    <div class="kpi-value">{kpis['decade_change_00s_10s']}%</div>
    <div class="kpi-unit">2000s → 2010s</div>
    <div class="kpi-label">Decade-over-Decade Change (Mean Rate)</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi-card">
    <div class="kpi-value">{kpis['current_coverage']} / {kpis['total_countries']}</div>
    <div class="kpi-unit">countries</div>
    <div class="kpi-label">Reporting Coverage ({kpis['max_year']})</div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- SECTION 1: GLOBAL OVERVIEW -->
<!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="section" id="global-overview">
  <h2>1. Global Homicide Rate Overview</h2>
  <p class="section-objective">Present the overall global trend in homicide rates from 1990 to 2023, including reporting coverage, global median and mean rates, and whether the world is becoming safer or more dangerous.</p>

  <h3>Key Finding: The World Is Becoming Safer, but Progress Is Uneven</h3>
  <p>The global <strong>median</strong> intentional homicide rate has declined substantially over the past three decades, from approximately <strong>3.35 per 100,000</strong> in 1990 to <strong>{kpis['global_median']} per 100,000</strong> in {kpis['max_year']} — a reduction of roughly <strong>45%</strong>. The mean rate has remained more volatile and elevated, driven by extreme outliers in a small number of high-violence countries. This divergence between median and mean underscores that while most countries have become safer, a subset of nations continues to experience severe violence.</p>

  <div class="chart-box">
    <div class="chart-title">Global Median &amp; Mean Homicide Rate, 1990–2023 (per 100,000 population)</div>
    <canvas id="chartGlobalTrend"></canvas>
  </div>

  <div class="callout">
    <strong>Interpretation:</strong> The median rate — a robust measure of central tendency that is not skewed by extreme outliers — shows a clear downward trajectory. The mean rate, however, has remained stubbornly high, reflecting persistent extreme violence in countries such as El Salvador, Honduras, Jamaica, and several Caribbean island nations. When the mean substantially exceeds the median, as it does here by a factor of 4–5x, it signals that homicide is <em>highly concentrated</em> in a small number of countries rather than being a broadly distributed global phenomenon.
  </div>

  <div class="chart-row">
    <div class="chart-box">
      <div class="chart-title">Number of Countries Reporting Homicide Data by Year</div>
      <canvas id="chartCoverage"></canvas>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-box">
      <div class="chart-title">Distribution of Homicide Rates by Year (Box Plot via Percentiles)</div>
      <canvas id="chartDistribution"></canvas>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p>Reporting coverage peaked at <strong>{kpis['peak_coverage']} countries</strong> in {kpis['peak_coverage_year']} but has since declined to <strong>{kpis['current_coverage']} countries</strong> in {kpis['max_year']}. This drop in reporting — particularly post-2020 — may reflect disruptions from the COVID-19 pandemic and should temper confidence in the most recent year's estimates. Fewer reporting countries means the median in 2023 is computed over a smaller and potentially different set of nations than in earlier years.</p>

  <div class="callout warning">
    <strong>Data Quality Note:</strong> The decline in reporting coverage from 162 countries (2008) to 84 (2023) means the most recent global median is based on roughly half the countries that reported at peak coverage. This compositional shift could bias apparent trends — if non-reporting countries tend to have higher (or lower) homicide rates than reporting countries, the true global median could differ from the reported figure.
  </div>

  <h3>Decade-by-Decade Averages</h3>
  <table class="data-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Decade</th><th>Mean Rate</th><th>Median Rate</th><th>Observations</th><th>Change in Mean</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>1990s</td><td>{kpis['decade_avgs']['1990s']}</td><td>3.96</td><td>1,012</td><td>—</td></tr>
      <tr><td>2000s</td><td>{kpis['decade_avgs']['2000s']}</td><td>3.33</td><td>1,385</td><td class="deteriorator">+2.9%</td></tr>
      <tr><td>2010s</td><td>{kpis['decade_avgs']['2010s']}</td><td>2.62</td><td>1,380</td><td class="improver">{kpis['decade_change_00s_10s']}%</td></tr>
      <tr><td>2020s</td><td>{kpis['decade_avgs']['2020s']}</td><td>2.35</td><td>438</td><td>+0.2% (partial)</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>The 2000s-to-2010s transition marked the largest improvement, with the <strong>global mean declining by {abs(kpis['decade_change_00s_10s'])}%</strong>. The median declined even more sharply — by <strong>{abs(kpis['decade_median_change'])}%</strong> — reinforcing that the improvement was broad-based rather than driven solely by a few large countries. The 2020s data is partial (only 4 years), but early indicators suggest stagnation rather than continued improvement.</p>
</div>

<!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- SECTION 2: REGIONAL & COUNTRY COMPARISON -->
<!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="section" id="regional-comparison">
  <h2>2. Regional &amp; Country-Level Comparison</h2>
  <p class="section-objective">Identify countries and regions with the highest and lowest homicide rates, highlight top and bottom 10 countries, and discuss geographic patterns.</p>

  <div class="chart-box">
    <div class="chart-title">Median Homicide Rate by Region, Most Recent Year ({kpis['max_year']})</div>
    <canvas id="chartRegionalBar"></canvas>
  </div>

  <div class="chart-row">
    <div class="chart-box">
      <div class="chart-title">Top 10 Countries — Highest Homicide Rates ({kpis['max_year']})</div>
      <canvas id="chartTop10"></canvas>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-box">
      <div class="chart-title">Bottom 10 Countries — Lowest Homicide Rates ({kpis['max_year']})</div>
      <canvas id="chartBottom10"></canvas>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3>Geographic Patterns</h3>
  <p>The data reveals a stark geographic concentration of homicide:</p>
  <ul class="insight-list">
    <li><strong>Latin America &amp; the Caribbean</strong> consistently exhibits the highest homicide rates globally. Caribbean island nations — particularly Saint Kitts and Nevis, Saint Vincent and the Grenadines, and Jamaica — occupy the top positions, with rates exceeding 40 per 100,000.</li>
    <li><strong>Africa</strong> shows elevated but highly variable rates, with data sparsity making robust regional estimates difficult. Available data suggests median rates in the 3–8 per 100,000 range for reporting countries.</li>
    <li><strong>East Asia &amp; Pacific</strong> demonstrates the lowest rates globally. Singapore, Japan, Hong Kong, and South Korea report rates below 0.5 per 100,000, representing some of the safest societies on earth.</li>
    <li><strong>Europe</strong> (all sub-regions) reports consistently low rates, with most countries below 2.0 per 100,000. Southern Europe is particularly safe, with Italy and Slovenia reporting rates under 0.6.</li>
    <li><strong>The Americas show extreme internal variation</strong>: the United States and Canada report moderate rates (2–6 per 100,000), while countries just to their south (Mexico, Honduras) report rates 5–15× higher.</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="chart-box">
    <div class="chart-title">Regional Median Homicide Rate Trends Over Time</div>
    <canvas id="chartRegionalTrends"></canvas>
  </div>

  <p>Regional trajectories show important divergence. Latin America &amp; the Caribbean has seen a pronounced <em>increase</em> over the past decade, diverging from other regions. Meanwhile, Eastern Europe experienced a dramatic decline after the post-Soviet crime wave of the 1990s — the regional median fell from over 8 per 100,000 in the mid-1990s to below 2.0 by the 2010s.</p>
</div>

<!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- SECTION 3: GENDER DISPARITY -->
<!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="section" id="sex-disparity">
  <h2>3. Gender Disparity in Homicide Victimization</h2>
  <p class="section-objective">Analyze the difference in homicide rates between males and females globally and across selected countries, quantifying the male-to-female ratio and how it has changed over time.</p>

  <h3>Key Finding: Men Are Killed at Approximately 3× the Rate of Women</h3>
